The test failures raise a very good question on how `MasterGameplayClockContainer` should actually behave when initially stopped in regards to current time and offsets.

On master, since `pauseFreqAdjust = 1` by default, `CreateGameplayClock` would initialise offset clocks and update their `RateAdjustedOffset` as well. Making the first gameplay start time seek in `LoadComplete` work properly.

Meanwhile on this PR, since `pauseFreqAdjust = 0` by default, `CreateGameplayClock` would initialise offset clocks with `RateAdjustedOffset` remaining to be zero. Making the first gameplay start time seek in `LoadComplete` become off by the applied offsets once GCC starts processing frames (even though the gameplay clock was not paused at `LoadComplete`).

For a solution, I think that whenever the state of `IsPaused` changes, `pauseFreqAdjust` should update immediately and process the offset clocks to update the `RateAdjustedOffset`, so that the first gameplay start time seek happens properly with `RateAdjustedOffset` being populated:
```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game/Screens/Play/GameplayClockContainer.cs b/osu.Game/Screens/Play/GameplayClockContainer.cs
index 226f5709c7..f2df00d691 100644
--- a/osu.Game/Screens/Play/GameplayClockContainer.cs
+++ b/osu.Game/Screens/Play/GameplayClockContainer.cs
@@ -122,14 +122,14 @@ public void Reset(bool startClock = false, double? gameplayStartTime = null)
             if (gameplayStartTime != null)
                 StartTime = gameplayStartTime;

-            ensureSourceClockSet();
-            Seek(StartTime ?? 0);
-
             // Manually stop the source in order to not affect the IsPaused state.
             AdjustableSource.Stop();

             if (!IsPaused.Value || startClock)
                 Start();
+
+            ensureSourceClockSet();
+            Seek(StartTime ?? 0);
         }

         /// <summary>
diff --git a/osu.Game/Screens/Play/MasterGameplayClockContainer.cs b/osu.Game/Screens/Play/MasterGameplayClockContainer.cs
index f4445d3fa0..2802f721c8 100644
--- a/osu.Game/Screens/Play/MasterGameplayClockContainer.cs
+++ b/osu.Game/Screens/Play/MasterGameplayClockContainer.cs
@@ -131,16 +131,29 @@ private double findEarliestStartTime()
         protected override void OnIsPausedChanged(ValueChangedEvent<bool> isPaused)
         {
             // The source is stopped by a frequency fade first.
-            if (isPaused.NewValue)
+            if (IsLoaded)
             {
-                this.TransformBindableTo(pauseFreqAdjust, 0, 200, Easing.Out).OnComplete(_ =>
+                if (isPaused.NewValue)
                 {
-                    if (IsPaused.Value == isPaused.NewValue)
-                        AdjustableSource.Stop();
-                });
+                    this.TransformBindableTo(pauseFreqAdjust, 0, 200, Easing.Out).OnComplete(_ =>
+                    {
+                        if (IsPaused.Value == isPaused.NewValue)
+                            AdjustableSource.Stop();
+                    });
+                }
+                else
+                    this.TransformBindableTo(pauseFreqAdjust, 1, 200, Easing.In);
             }
             else
-                this.TransformBindableTo(pauseFreqAdjust, 1, 200, Easing.In);
+            {
+                pauseFreqAdjust.Value = isPaused.NewValue ? 0 : 1;
+
+                if (isPaused.NewValue)
+                    AdjustableSource.Stop();
+
+                // process underlying gameplay clocks to update rate-adjusted offsets with the new frequency adjustment.
+                GameplayClock.UnderlyingClock.ProcessFrame();
+            }
         }

         public override void Start()
```

The above diff also reorders `Reset` such that it updates the running state of the clock before performing a seek, for the `RateAdjustedOffset` values to be updated properly for correct seeking.

---

Have confirmed that the above patch passes all tests.
